course: dictionary
lesson: 8337
title: A small language with a big story
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can name a language, a place, or a group of people. When you read «Romansh», look at the words around it to see which one it is. In the sentence below, the clues are «national languages» and «Switzerland», so Romansh is a language.
explain: «Switzerland has four national languages, German, French, Italian and Romansh; French is spoken in the west, around Geneva (Genève) and Lausanne.» The list tells you that Romansh is one of four languages used across the whole country. The word «French» in the same sentence is a clue too: it shows that each language can be spoken in a different part of Switzerland.
explain: Romansh is also used as an adjective, a word that describes a noun. «Romansh speakers» means the people who speak Romansh. «In Romansh» means using that language. Ask yourself: does the word name a thing, or does it describe one? That tells you how it works in the sentence.
fact: Romansh is a language spoken by a small number of people in south-east Switzerland, in the canton of Graubünden.
fact: Romansh is one of Switzerland's four national languages, with German, French and Italian.
fact: Romansh comes from Latin, like French, Italian and Spanish.
fact: Fewer than 1 in 100 Swiss people speak Romansh as their main language, so it is a small language.
fact: As an adjective, Romansh means to do with this language or its speakers, as in «Romansh speakers».
exercise: «Switzerland has four national languages, German, French, Italian and Romansh.» How many national languages does Switzerland have? | Three | Five | Two | *Four
exercise: In the sentence, which language is spoken in the west, around Geneva and Lausanne? | *French | German | Italian | Romansh
exercise: What is Romansh? | *A language spoken in south-east Switzerland | A type of Swiss cheese | A city near Geneva | A mountain in Graubünden
test: Romansh comes from which older language? | Greek | Sanskrit | Old English | *Latin
test: In which canton is Romansh spoken? | *Graubünden | Geneva | Ticino | Vaud
exam: Which statement about Romansh is true? | Romansh is spoken by most people in Switzerland | *Romansh is one of Switzerland's four national languages | Romansh is spoken in France | Romansh is the main language of Geneva
